# Herd (local stack)

Laravel Herd Pro is the only local set-up (decided 14 November 2026, #282; Laragon was replaced earlier, #213 / #344). Never suggest containers, virtual machines, Laragon as current practice, or `php artisan serve`. Do not use Herd's badge or app "dev" stack (`php artisan dev`): it clashes with Vite on 5174 and removes `public/hot` when it stops. Use `scripts\preview.ps1` and `npm run dev` instead.

Values: `docs/herd/profile.json`. Guide: `docs/local-development.md`. Site is HTTPS (`https://apes-intranet.test`, via `herd secure apes-intranet`).

## Tools

- Herd MCP (`user-herd`) serves this site as `apes-intranet`: `site` `info` / `error`, `logs` `read`, `insights`, `mail`, and `env` (masks secrets).
- Mail: Herd catcher SMTP `127.0.0.1:2525` (never sent).
- `herd which-php apes-intranet` must print Herd's `php84` build. If not: `herd isolate 8.4 --site=apes-intranet`.

## Ask first

- `php artisan demo:reset` (empties the local database), or installing any system tool (PHP version/extension, Herd service, Node version).
- Ad-hoc migrations outside `scripts\preview.ps1` / `scripts\herd-setup.ps1` (those scripts already run pending migrations locally).
- Changing Herd's global PHP, `php.ini`, or a service port.

## Cloudron safety (local vs server)

- `public/.htaccess` is for Cloudron's Apache (nginx ignores it locally): no `php_value` / `php_flag` outside `<IfModule php_module>` (local equivalents in `public/.user.ini`); keep the `HTTP_AUTHORIZATION` rewrite rule.
- Test with fake demo data via Developer sign-in on <https://apes-intranet.test/login> (QA pill / `/qa` fallback).
